# Microsoft Entra ID – Enterprise Applications & Single Sign-On (SSO)

## 🧩 Overview

This lab demonstrates how to configure Enterprise Applications and Single Sign-On (SSO) using Microsoft Entra ID.

Enterprise Applications allow organizations to centrally manage user access to third-party applications while providing secure authentication through Single Sign-On.

In this lab, an Enterprise Application was configured, users were assigned, and Single Sign-On was enabled to provide seamless access to cloud resources using Microsoft Entra ID credentials.

---

# ⚠️ Real-World Risk

Without Enterprise Applications and Single Sign-On:

- Users manage multiple passwords.
- Password reuse increases security risks.
- User onboarding and offboarding become difficult.
- Access management becomes inconsistent.

Enterprise Applications and SSO help organizations:

✅ Centralize application access

✅ Reduce password fatigue

✅ Improve security posture

✅ Streamline user provisioning

✅ Strengthen identity governance

